  "recap": "The Base Invaders' bats were far from silent on Wednesday, August 26, but the Expos simply outscored them in a 22-6 shootout. It's hard to complain about a night with 18 team hits and 9 different players reaching base, yet the defense and pitching couldn't keep pace with what turned into a track meet. Erik led the way going a perfect 4-for-4, with Jason right behind him at 3-for-4 and Vee matching that pace at 3-for-3. Brandon added a home run and an RBI while going 2-for-4, and Dallas chipped in a 2-for-3 night with an RBI of his own. The offense showed up in a big way — the Base Invaders just need the rest of the game to catch up next time out.",
